  annotation "note_1771592856704_0", anchor: "a habit drilled deep enough to outlast her direct instruction", text: "Hammers lined by weight. Of everything in this entry — the scars, the testimony, the silences — this is what will survive. Not because it matters most, but because it lives in other penguins' flippers now. The ice preserves grand things and terrible things. Habit preserves the rest.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771592856704_1", anchor: "which she entered once and does not discuss", text: "There is a specific quality to silence earned beneath the Berg. Not secrecy — secrecy implies something worth protecting. This is the silence of having seen a thing that rearranged the terms under which you understand yourself. My left flipper carries a frost-scar from the Whisper Galleries. The Nightshelf sent a formal apology I have not opened. I recognize the grammar of her refusal. I did not press when drafting this entry. Some thresholds you do not ask another penguin to cross twice.", type: :tangent, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771592856704_2", anchor: "Neither crossed the threshold between them", text: "The Compass of Crystal appears in current damage inventories — thirteen segments, awaiting restoration or destruction. Zheishongfeihua offered a broken artifact to someone who would understand what the thirteenth segment cost. That neither of them moved closer is not ceremony. It is two penguins who know what shared corruption feels like standing at exactly the distance where recognition does not become contagion.", type: :commentary, display: :full
